    <Program class="ca.nrcan.gc.OEE.ERS.ErsProgram">
        <Labels>
            <English>EnerGuide Rating System</English>
            <French>Système de cote ÉnerGuide</French>
        </Labels>
        <Version major="15" minor="1" build="19">
            <Labels>
                <English>v15.1b19</English>
                <French>v15.1b19</French>
            </Labels>
        </Version>
        <SdkVersion major="1" minor="11">
            <Labels>
                <English>v1.11</English>
                <French>v1.11</French>
            </Labels>
        </SdkVersion>
        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air leakage can be one of the largest causes of heat loss in a home. Listed below are some following areas that can be improved:



Electrical Receptacles

Heat Registers

Chimney

Water Line-In

Fondation/Main Floor Wall Intercept

Pot Lights

Bathroom Fan

Plumbing Rough-Ins

Electrical Panel

Basement Wall Cracks

Window and Door Returns (During Renovations)

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>The main walls and gable end walls show potential for improvement. An upgrade of R-20  by applying 4" of EPS to the exterior of the wall. Usually you would not get R-20 from 4" of EPS, but a product called Halo Xterra has a nomial insulation value of R-5/inch. Choosing EPS over XPS is more enviromentally friendly because of the embodied energy of the product.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings />
                <ceilingsCathedral>The enitre roof should have R-50 of rigid board added on the exterior. The shingles are old and need to be replaced as well. This addition will make the 5 foot area on each side on the house (second floor) which is accessable by a small door, part of the building envelope.</ceilingsCathedral>
                <foundation>Fix any cracks in the foundation. Basement windows could be upgraded to triple glazed, low-E, argon filled, vinyl windows. You could also just take the windows out entirely and get the spaces filled in. 



Foundation Floor:

The basement height is only 7' which makes a concern for usuable space. Add 1" XPS at R-5 to the floor. This will improve insualtion levels and comfort while keeping usuable space in the forefront. 



Foundation Walls:

The exterior wall should have the same R-20 EPS added to the exterior. This should only extend halway down the exterior of the wall. A 2x4 wall with R-12 batt insulation should be added to the interior on the wall. You will not lose much usuable space and will still be adding insulation and improving comfort.



</foundation>
                <windows>Windows are outdated and should be upgraded to:



 Triple Glazed, 2 layers low-E, Argon filled, inusulated spacer, vinyl windows</windows>
                <doors>Both Doors should be upgraded to steel doors with medium density spray foam core. Windows in doors should be triple glazed with one layer of low-E, and gas filled.</doors>
                <VentilationSystem>Add a HRV to improve air qualtiy in the home and to help with any pressure issues in the home.</VentilationSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
